<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RMS Props half yr headline shr edges up.</title>
<headline>RMS Props half yr headline shr edges up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Earnings per linked unit (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		29.14	 vs 28.91</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 0.29	  vs 0.29</p>
<p>Interest per debenture (cts)</p>
<p>				  28.85	 vs 28.62</p>
<p>    After tax profit	2.54	  vs 0.12</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2.55	  vs 0.13</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.02	  vs 0.02</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   11.47	 vs 11.38</p>
<p>    Turnover		  16.26	 vs 16.05</p>
<p>Div payable May 23</p>
<p>on register May 9</p>
<p>Full name: RMS Property Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The total distribution for the whole year is expected to be about 10 percent higher than last yar, directors said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
